# immich-curator documentation workflow

When planning or implementing features in this repo:

1. Start from [docs/README.md](../../docs/README.md).
2. Ensure traceability: user story → use case → design → ADR (if architectural) → implementation plan → code.
3. Use naming conventions in docs/README (US-, UC-, DES-, ADR NNNN, IP-YYYY-MM-DD-).
4. Immich API: server-side only per [docs/adr/0001-server-side-immich-api.md](../../docs/adr/0001-server-side-immich-api.md).
5. Engineering: [docs/adr/0003-tech-stack-and-engineering-practices.md](../../docs/adr/0003-tech-stack-and-engineering-practices.md)—current stack practices, simplicity, single code paths, token theme, libraries, proportionate TDD.
6. Do not add Poundsgate migration or Ian-owned-library assumptions unless a new ADR supersedes 0001.

For Next.js specifics, follow the `nextjs-agent-rules` block in [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md).

**Cache Components (App Router):** Before editing routes under `src/app/(app)/`, read the Cursor skill [.cursor/skills/immich-curator-cache-components/SKILL.md](../../.cursor/skills/immich-curator-cache-components/SKILL.md) so Suspense boundaries, URL data, and `connection()` match Next 16 + `cacheComponents` expectations.

**Runtime:** **Development** — run `npm run dev` and verify against that server (resolve port 3000 vs systemd as in [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md)). **Production** — keep **`immich-curator`** user systemd active (`systemctl --user status immich-curator`); after app code changes that should hit the deployed app, **run** `npm run build && systemctl --user restart immich-curator` in the agent session right away (not a “pull then you run it” note).
